I wrote the DropSeen node, but left out both operations requests. The node's only granted capability is `aap:caps/state-read`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need filesystem and HTTP authority it doesn't hold. The metadata fetch would also send feed text to an outside service. If you want either, the graph needs to grant the node an `http-client` or `notifier` capability first.

An item is dropped when `state-read.get` returns a value for its `id`, and kept otherwise. Input order is preserved.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

